# PART 3 — DATASET STRATEGY

Use multiple real industrial anomaly detection datasets.

The datasets must remain independently identifiable, independently configurable, and independently evaluated.

Never blindly merge different datasets into one training set.

## DATASET A — MVTec AD

Official page:

https://www.mvtec.com/research-teaching/datasets/mvtec-ad

Role:
Primary benchmark.

It contains over 5,000 images across 15 object and texture categories, with normal training samples, normal and anomalous test images, and pixel-precise anomaly masks.

Use all 15 categories where resources allow.

Prioritize initial implementation and validation using:

- bottle
- screw
- metal_nut
- capsule
- cable
- hazelnut

Expand to remaining categories after the pipeline is verified.

Respect its CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 license.

## DATASET B — VisA

Official AWS Open Data registry:

https://registry.opendata.aws/visa/

Project documentation:

https://github.com/amazon-research/spot-diff

Role:
Independent multi-category industrial benchmark.

It contains 10,821 images across 12 object categories, including normal and anomalous samples with image-level and pixel-level annotations.

Use its documented dataset preparation and split protocol.

License: CC BY 4.0 as identified by its official registry.

Implement a dedicated VisA data adapter.

Do not assume its folder layout matches MVTec AD.

## DATASET C — MVTec LOCO AD

Official page:

https://www.mvtec.com/research-teaching/datasets/mvtec-loco-ad

Role:
Advanced logical and structural anomaly evaluation.

It contains five categories and includes both structural defects and logical anomalies.

Use this dataset to investigate the limitations of appearance-based methods.

Respect CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

Do not assume every logical anomaly can be accurately localized using pixel-level texture methods.

## DATASET D — MVTec AD 2

Official page:

https://www.mvtec.com/research-teaching/datasets/mvtec-ad-2

Role:
Advanced robustness and challenging inspection conditions.

Investigate its official public evaluation data and supported evaluation protocol.

The private evaluation data must not be accessed or inferred from.

Use only data that is officially available to the project.

Respect CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

## OPTIONAL DATASET E — BTAD

Investigate the BeanTech Anomaly Detection dataset.

Use it only if:

- An authoritative source can be verified.
- The dataset can legally be obtained.
- Its license and redistribution conditions are documented.
- Its annotation format can be supported correctly.

Do not block the main project if BTAD access is unavailable.

